        "id": 3494485
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-03T04:57:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The behavior of the host without pKVM is to do nothing (returning 0) as in the function [device_pasid_table_setup](https://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v6.12.42/source/drivers/iommu/intel/pasid.c#L776) which is the inspiration for this change. \nThe correct behavior of the host should be to clear the context entry first and then put the right entry, so the host shouldn\u0027t be allowed to change the context entry without clearing it first.\n\nReturning -EBUSY seems equally valid or maybe better. What do you suggest?",
      "parentUuid": "5d169d39_8e8a1892",
      "revId": "aec99fde482f2dca1b31c1e95dbe5d09bb5f6610",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d9f84b7_131dd9f5",
