        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-03T20:33:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The behavior of the host without pKVM is to do nothing (returning 0) as in the function device_pasid_table_setup which is the inspiration for this change.\n\nI see, indeed. And I see the host has the same behavior for legacy mode entries as well (e.g. in domain_context_mapping_one()). And I see this behavior dates back to the very first revision of Intel IOMMU driver in 2007...\n\nSo, I don\u0027t know... I\u0027d suggest at least to keep it consistent with legacy mode, i.e. either return -EBUSY in both, or return 0 in both.\n\nAs for which is better, -EBUSY or 0... Now it seems to me that actually 0 is better, to be compatible with the host driver\u0027s expectations?",
      "parentUuid": "50f9362d_e95b91f8",
      "revId": "aec99fde482f2dca1b31c1e95dbe5d09bb5f6610",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
