      "writtenOn": "2025-11-29T19:25:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027ve donated the context table page in pkvm_iommu_context_addr() above, we\u0027d better undonate it before returning error here?",
      "revId": "aec99fde482f2dca1b31c1e95dbe5d09bb5f6610",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e6cd8453_bebac400",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/pv_iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 46
      },
      "lineNbr": 339,
      "author": {
        "id": 3494485
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-03T04:57:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These paths are independent. There are two cases:\n\nContext page (which contains dev/fns for a particular bus) exists: The page for this bus is already present (shared by other devices on this bus), so un-donating doesn\u0027t make sense.\n\nContext page missing: We install the page provided in param-\u003econtext_gpa before. This donated page is now active and can serve other dev/fns on the same bus later, or a future call for the same dev/fn may too succeed. Most likely, it fails due to a bug in pKVM or a host being malicious.",
      "parentUuid": "a1fb65b4_95a10ae6",
      "revId": "aec99fde482f2dca1b31c1e95dbe5d09bb5f6610",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "197931b7_c0f66b76",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/pv_iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 46
      },
      "lineNbr": 339,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-03T20:33:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Context page missing: We install the page provided in param-\u003econtext_gpa before. This donated page is now active and can serve other dev/fns on the same bus later, or a future call for the same dev/fn may too succeed.\n\nYeah, we already discussed this with Vineeth in another thread, and now it seems clear to me that in the specific case of (pkvm_)iommu_context_addr() we basically have \"global lazy\" allocation of context entries, so even if we failed after we successfully allocated and donated a context entry, it makes sense to keep it allocated and donated, instead of trying to gracefully undonate it in the error path.",
      "parentUuid": "e6cd8453_bebac400",
      "revId": "aec99fde482f2dca1b31c1e95dbe5d09bb5f6610",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
